sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant R as Runner (code)
    participant A as Reviewer A
    participant B as Reviewer B
    participant C as Reviewer C
    participant V as Verifier (code)
    participant S as Second look
    participant P as Human reviewer

    Note over R: Titles: batches of 50 titles, sent before the graph runs
    par independent, blind
        R->>A: 50 titles + codebook (persona: neurologist)
        R->>B: 50 titles + codebook (persona: ML researcher)
        R->>C: 50 titles + codebook (persona: methodologist)
    end
    A-->>R: per title: rule marks + quotes
    B-->>R: per title: rule marks + quotes
    C-->>R: per title: rule marks + quotes
    R->>V: every quote must be in the title
    Note over R: excluded only if all 3 exclude

    Note over R: Abstracts: batches of 4 (Groq, OpenRouter when Groq is busy)
    par independent, blind
        R->>A: 4 abstracts
        R->>B: 4 abstracts
        R->>C: 4 abstracts
    end
    A-->>R: rule marks + quotes
    B-->>R: rule marks + quotes
    C-->>R: rule marks + quotes
    R->>V: quotes checked, no quote means unclear
    Note over R: weighted majority, 2-1 exclusions flagged

    Note over R: Full text (free copies only), one paper per call
    par independent, blind
        R->>A: whole paper (Nemotron 3 Ultra)
        R->>B: whole paper (Gemma 4 31B)
        R->>C: whole paper (dots.3)
    end
    A-->>R: include / exclude / unclear + quotes
    B-->>R: include / exclude / unclear + quotes
    C-->>R: include / exclude / unclear + quotes
    R->>V: quotes checked
    Note over R: majority, unclear or no majority goes on

    opt paper left unclear
        R->>S: same paper + the rules the panel left open (not the votes)
        S-->>R: include / exclude / unclear + quotes
        opt still unclear
            R->>P: paper, all votes, quotes, reasoning (stages.xlsx)
            P-->>R: decision
        end
    end
